From c267bb00061bf5abaa3e1ac264ae46cfca441115 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cgscli <cgscli@localhost>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:13:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] P13: attach a remote to a live TUI session; the terminal
 stands by and takes over on Esc

Reason: A remote must see and drive a terminal session with the same frames a headless rpc-ui process speaks. The RPC dispatcher is wired to stdio and the process lifetime, and the TUI has no notion of an outside controller. The extension API reaches neither, so the dispatcher is factored (attachRpcMode), a `tui_attach` extension event hands the channel to the extension that serves it (cgsconnect), and the terminal gates its own keys and commands while a remote controls the session (ADR 0027).
Upstream: none (CGS remote access)
Remove-when: upstream offers a way for extensions to attach an RPC channel to an interactive session and to arbitrate control

- rpc-mode.ts: runRpcMode's dispatcher is createRpcDispatcher; attachRpcMode runs it on a live session over a send callback, without owning the process; dialogs it shows are handed to the terminal's UI when the attachment closes
- StandbyController: single control end, Esc takeover (1 press: takeover, 2: stop, 3: rewind), `taken_over` line sent first, default-deny command and key allowlists
- InteractiveMode: `tui_attach` event after the extension hooks, red right-aligned hint, standby gate in the composer and global key paths and before a submission; ExtensionRunner.setUIContext swaps the UI extension dialogs use
